//// A project cell narrows itself with `"targets"` in its `botopink.json`, the
//// way a `run/` cell does with `<name>.targets` — and the narrowing stands on
//// the same evidence: `magnitude` is bound for the BEAM alone, so commonJS and
//// wasm REFUSE the project (``has no `#[@External.<Target>(…)]` ``), which
//// `run.sh` checks on every run. The cell runs on erlang and beam, and nowhere
//// else; a `"targets"` the compiler did not back would fail the run.
////
//// The binding is declared in the entry: an IMPORTED host function with no
//// binding for the target is not refused by commonJS yet (the call dies with
//// `magnitude is not a function`) nor located by erlang — rows of those
//// backends' fronts, which this cell must not stand on.

pub mod text;
import {label} from "text";

#[@External.Erlang("erlang", "abs")]
declare fn magnitude(n: i32) -> i32;

pub fn main() {
    @print(label(magnitude(0 - 7)));
}
